    "c3": {
      "anchor": "p-quoted-words-on-tags#field-5",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Quoted Words On Tags",
      "excerpt": "Let a quoted word be contents. In the tokenizer, a tag in the list can say its q",
      "text": "this should be <header \"Hardware\" icon=\"...\"/>",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-09T15:34:12.565Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "<header \"Hardware\"><icon/></header>",
      "offset": 788,
      "edited": "2026-11-09T15:34:16.899Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T15:41:02.674Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded in. <code>&lt;header \"Hardware\" icon=\"gear\"/&gt;</code> will work: <code>icon</code> on a header takes a name, as a button's does, and draws it before the text. That's the one Spell UI change in this phase, and the plan now says so. A bare <code>icon</code> keeps its large centred layout. The example of a word with other contents is now <code>&lt;label \"Inbox\"&gt;&lt;detail&gt;3&lt;/detail&gt;&lt;/label&gt;</code>.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
